Turnip: don't force per-sample interpolation when sample shading is on.

MrPurple666's T30 (clean MK8 menu icons in Eden on A722) always leaves
tu_shader_key::force_sample_interp false; upstream sets it whenever
sampleShadingEnable is set, so every non-centroid FS input is evaluated
at its sample position. Eden's MSAA blits (blit_color_msaa.frag:
texelFetch(tex, ivec2(texcoord), gl_SampleID), sampleShadingEnable with
minSampleShading 1.0) then fetch different source texels per sample when
the blit is scaled. Match T30.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_pipeline.cc
@@ -1945,6 +1945,6 @@
        * just checked in tu6_emit_fs_inputs.  We will also copy the value to
        * tu_shader_key::force_sample_interp in a bit.
        */
-      keys[MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT].force_sample_interp =
-         !builder->rasterizer_discard && msaa_info && msaa_info->sampleShadingEnable;
+      /* Like MrPurple T30: Eden's MSAA blits expect pixel-center inputs. */
+      keys[MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT].force_sample_interp = false;
    }
